' Recommended pipeline for cost-accounted (v6) shards: order-then-execute.
' Consensus orders accepted envelopes and never waits for execution. A
' deterministic executor runs the finalized order, applies the P1 acceptance
' gate before each envelope, and settles it. Later blocks attest the executed
' roots, and a wrong attestation is slashing evidence.
'
' Paper anchors: P1 = publications cost-accounting/cost-accounted-rho.tex
'   gate P1:2188-2213 · rejection without effect P1:2208-2212 ·
'   block validity P1:1708-1714 · epoch boundary P1:3036-3043.
' Source of truth: docs/casper/theory/cost-accounting-consensus-proposal.md §7.
' Palette: user and envelope = supply blue · proposer = control amber ·
'   gate and inclusion filter = gate teal · Casper core = capability indigo ·
'   linearizer = process lilac · executor = pool green ·
'   attested roots = delta orange · rejection = reject red
' The legend also defines every name and abbreviation that the labels use,
' so the diagram reads on its own.
' Render:  ./render.sh consensus-proposal-order-then-execute.puml

@startuml consensus-proposal-order-then-execute
!include palette.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor              $ca_neutral
  LifeLineBorderColor     #666666
  ParticipantBorderColor  #333333
  DividerBackgroundColor  $ca_note_grey
  GroupBorderColor        #666666
  GroupBackgroundColor    #FAFAFA
}
skinparam maxMessageSize 330
title Recommended for v6 shards: order-then-execute

autonumber

actor       "User\n(signer)"                             as U  $ca_supply
participant "Proposer\n(no execution)"                    as P  $ca_control
participant "Inclusion filter\n(DR-64 check, DR-65 groups)" as G $ca_gate
participant "Validators\n(structural validity)"           as V  $ca_capability
participant "Fork choice and\nclique-oracle finality"     as F  $ca_capability
participant "Linearizer\n(main-chain epochs)"             as L  $ca_process
participant "Executor\n(P1 gate, execute, settle)"        as X  $ca_pool
database    "Executed roots\nand attestations"            as A  $ca_delta

== Inclusion: the proposer orders and does not execute ==
U -[$ca_instantiate]> P : signed offered envelope
P -> A : newest finalized block E that this node\nhas executed, and its root <latex>r_E</latex>
P -> G : candidates in canonical order
G -> G : DR-64 check of each envelope at <latex>r_E</latex>,\nDR-65 group rule inside the block,\nper-block demand cap
G --> P : included envelopes
P -[$ca_instantiate]> V : block = parents, justifications, envelopes,\nattestation <latex>(E, r_E)</latex>, epoch validator set

== Structural validation: no merge, no replay ==
V -> V : signature, sequence number, justifications,\nequivocation check (unchanged Casper)
V -> V : envelope syntax and signatures, validity window,\nrepeat rule in the past cone, demand cap,\nempty v6 merge fields
V -> F : add the valid block to the DAG
note over P, F $ca_note_green
  **Consensus keeps accepting blocks.** No step of
  inclusion or validation waits for execution
  (P1:1708-1714 makes block validity a syntactic predicate).
end note

== Finality: unchanged Casper ==
F -> F : LMD-GHOST fork choice with the invalid-message\nfilter, clique oracle with the epoch weights
F -> L : the LFB advances, the newly finalized set

== Deterministic linearization ==
L -> L : for each new main-chain block M: the blocks of\n<latex>\mathrm{past}(M) \setminus \mathrm{past}(\mathrm{mp}(M))</latex> in topological order,\nties broken by (block number, block hash)
L -> X : ordered blocks, each with its envelopes in block order

== Execution after finality ==
loop each envelope e in the canonical order
  X -> X : e already executed, or outside its validity window?\nThen skip e with no effect.
  X -> X : P1 gate at the current root: <latex>\Sigma_s \geq \Delta_s</latex> for every lane s?\n(DR-65 group rule for members of one block)
  alt the gate accepts
    X -> X : hold, execute, settle: charge measured use,\nrefund the unused hold, fee to the including proposer
  else the gate rejects
    X -[$ca_debit]> X : reject e: no state change,\nno tokens consumed (P1:2208-2212)
  end
end
X -> X : CloseBlock and slash system work of each block\nat its position in the order
X -> A : record (block, root) for each executed block

== Attestation and deferred checks ==
P -> A : the next proposal reads its newest executed root
P -[$ca_instantiate]> V : the next block attests <latex>(E', r_{E'})</latex>
V -> A : when local execution reaches <latex>E'</latex>:\ncompare the attested root and re-run the\ninclusion filter of that block at its attested root
note over V, A $ca_note_red
  A root mismatch, or an envelope that fails the filter at the
  proposer's own attested root, is signed slashing evidence.
  It never changes block validity after the fact.
end note

legend bottom
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<$ca_supply>| user and signed envelope |
  |<$ca_control>| proposer |
  |<$ca_gate>| DR-64 check and inclusion filter |
  |<$ca_capability>| Casper core: validity, DAG, fork choice, finality |
  |<$ca_process>| deterministic linearization |
  |<$ca_pool>| execution after finality |
  |<$ca_delta>| executed roots and attestations |
  |<$ca_note_red>| slashing evidence |

  |= name |= meaning |
  | P1 | the paper "Cost-Accounted Rho Calculus" (L. G. Meredith, May 2026). P1:a-b cites its lines a to b. |
  | P1 gate | accept an envelope only if <latex>\Sigma_s \geq \Delta_s</latex> for every signature lane s |
  | <latex>\Sigma_s</latex>, <latex>\Delta_s</latex> | the token supply and the demand of signature s |
  | DR-64 | the decision record of the funding check before execution |
  | DR-65 | the decision record that makes same-block offers on one purse one funding decision |
  | E, <latex>r_E</latex> | the newest finalized block that the proposer has executed, and its root. E' is a later one. |
  | e | one envelope: a signed user deploy |
  | M, mp(M), past(M) | a main-chain block, its main parent, and M with all its ancestors |
  | LMD-GHOST | latest-message-driven greedy heaviest-observed subtree fork choice |
  | LFB, DAG | the last finalized block, and the directed acyclic graph of blocks |
  | v6 | protocol version 6, with cost accounting |
  | CloseBlock | the system deploy that closes each block |
endlegend

@enduml
